<https://sws.geonames.org/3017382/>
        a       ecrm:E53_Place .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/3ed39219-d13a-3bfa-8c8a-1fd47159511e/observation/5>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man’s coat and waistcoat\nAbout 1760–80\n\nA fashionable man would have worn these garments in the city during the day, perhaps when shopping. He would have bought the fine wool from a draper and taken it to a tailor to be made into a bespoke three-piece suit with breeches. The eye-catching red cloth is set off by a subtly revealed sky-blue lining and silver spangled buttons.\n\nProbably France\nWool; silk twill and linen lining\nButtons: foiled metal, embroidered with silver spangles and thread\n [09/12/2015]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3ed39219-d13a-3bfa-8c8a-1fd47159511e> .

<http://data.silknow.org/collection/461f5c7a-9b6a-38ab-ab63-fe453c1336b3>
