<http://data.silknow.org/object/99265aad-31dc-37f6-9b95-4cebd29f6f25>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "Hart, Avril and Susan North. <i>Historical Fashion in Detail: The 17th and 18th Centuries</i>. London: V&A Publications, 1998. p. 98\n\nBaumgarten, Linda, <i>What Clothes Reveal. The Language of Clothing in Colonial and Federal America</i>, Yale University Press, 2002, p. 79. A coat made in Massachussetts of red wool broadcloth about 1770. The cut is similar though it has a turn down collar and no decorative finish.\nFlorence Montgomery. <i>Textiles in America 1650-1880</i>, Norton: New York, 1984, pp.177-8. For discussion of British broadcloth."@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3ed39219-d13a-3bfa-8c8a-1fd47159511e> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Hart, Avril and Susan North. <i>Historical Fashion in Detail: The 17th and 18th Centuries</i>. London: V&A Publications, 1998. p. 98\n\nBaumgarten, Linda, <i>What Clothes Reveal. The Language of Clothing in Colonial and Federal America</i>, Yale University Press, 2002, p. 79. A coat made in Massachussetts of red wool broadcloth about 1770. The cut is similar though it has a turn down collar and no decorative finish.\nFlorence Montgomery. <i>Textiles in America 1650-1880</i>, Norton: New York, 1984, pp.177-8. For discussion of British broadcloth."@en .

